            <ArticleTitle>[Surgical emergency disclosing sarcoidosis. Apropos of a case].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>196-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sarcoidosis is a diffuse granulomatosis predominately with mediastino-pulmonary localizations. A wide range of extrathoracic localizations can also occur and when they are the initial manifestation, may lead to misdiagnosis. We observed a rare case of peritoneal sarcoidosis revealed by a surgical emergency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
